In mathematics, a prime number is| a countable number whose prime number is 1 (and is not divisible by 3 or smaller). More precisely, there are two numbers that are prime, namely, 2 and 3.
In this class, we will try to demonstrate that if we are able to make a prime number, we can be able to find all of the other numbers of the first type that are prime. There are many more prime numbers, of course, but we will not focus on them here.
